  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In white crane sea area she laughs when Fairy You Chan finally comes to her. Narration names her owner of that sea area and one of Eastern Sea’s six beauties. She does not like men and only likes female immortals. She keeps a rank six Immortal Gu House called Bai He Palace there as her harem of women, and she grabs You Chan’s hands with an indulgent claim that You Chan will stay with her from that day on.",
      "chapters": [
        1483
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_you_chan",
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_bai_he_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is extremely beautiful and tall, with an elegant neck and long legs.",
      "chapters": [
        1483
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She works with You Chan for half a month on silver dragonfish breeding, helped by Heavenly Court findings and Fang Yuan’s silver dragonfish, and celebrates when their method improves so production can rise.",
      "chapters": [
        1484
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "silver-dragonfish-work",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With her and You Chan dead, Eastern Sea is left with only four of its six fairies, and Fang Yuan takes both their immortal apertures out and seals them temporarily so he can carry them with him. Disguised as her by familiar face, he is let into her rank six Immortal Gu House Bai He Palace, where only her own will remains, and he captures that will before taking the house apart for its two rank six Immortal Gu, one wood path and the other food path Eat Fragrance. Bai He Palace is fragile and far weaker than Hei tribe’s Dark Prison. He kills every concubine inside the palace as he disassembles it, leaving only their souls. He lands her rank seven wood path immortal aperture in an unnamed Eastern Sea sea area, where it turns into Bai He blessed land, and rather than meet its land spirit’s condition, which has to do with Bai He Palace, he suppresses the land spirit with blood light spirit suppression. He cannot annex a wood path blessed land, so he leaves it standing there, safe enough while its entrance is closed, and its resources are already destroyed as he expected.",
      "chapters": [
        1487
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "bai-he-palace-and-her-blessed-land",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_eat_fragrance_immortal_gu",
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "house_dark_prison"
      ]
    }
  ],
